  "body": "Replacement for PR 1310 by seelesturm (their fork does not accept maintainer pushes; the author asked for the resolution to be applied). Their commits are kept unchanged; the only addition is one merge of main.\n\n## What the merge resolved\n\n- `xtask/src/main.rs` mod block: kept the PR's layout and added every module main has (`merge_delta`, `merge_plan`, `merge_plan_git`, `merge_plan_out`, and the `#[cfg(test)]` modules `merge_plan_tests`, `merge_plan_det_tests`, `package_paths_tests`); each declared once, all files in `xtask/src` checked.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`: main is at 58; open PR 1418 holds 59, so this takes 60.\n- Nothing else conflicted; `git diff origin/main --stat` lists only the PR's own 13 files.\n\n## Gate results (native Windows, worktree at merged head)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (plan: xtask unit tests only); `cargo test -p xtask`: 112 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run` on this head vs the same dry-run on origin/main: plans identical (same suites and binaries; only the log timestamp differs). `gate quick --dry-run --base origin/main` names the xtask unit tests.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nApplication, full and release suites; other platforms; no hosted workflow. No snapshot or golden touched.\n\nChangelog: xtask recognizes directory test suites and keeps quick and named test selection scoped to their qualified tests.\n\nFixes #927\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
